__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Policy: every research artifact this pipeline produces is committed -- the
# Stage 1 reference snapshot, the full GA scored population, and the complete
# per-candidate gate4 alignment and tree output that earlier revisions excluded.
# Only three classes remain ignored: third-party binaries, solver scratch state
# that is not a result, and the two top-level pipeline logs. Each is explained
# at its rule below.
#
# Measured cost of tracking the rest (2026-10-13). The headline 498 MB of gate4
# tree files is misleading on two counts:
#   * 53.6% of those 740 files are byte-identical across candidates, and Git
#     stores content once -- 498 MB of files is 231 MB of distinct blobs.
#   * FASTA, .mldist and .phy are text and pack at 3.6x, so those 231 MB pack
#     to 26 MB. The snapshot's 74 MB of JSON packs to 7 MB (10.6x).
# Net pack growth ~34 MB, taking the repository from 295 MB to ~329 MB. That is
# comfortably inside every GitHub limit (100 MB per file, 2 GB per push, 5 GB
# per repository; largest file here is 27.5 MB). Re-measure with:
#     git count-objects -vH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# External tool binaries: 38 MB of downloadable archives plus their extracted trees.
# The pin is recorded by tools/CHECKSUMS.sha256 and tools/VERSIONS.txt, which ARE
# tracked -- committing the artifacts themselves would bloat the repo to no purpose.
tools/dist/
tools/mafft-win/
tools/iqtree-3.1.3-Windows/
tools/_download_meta.json

# IQ-TREE resume checkpoints -- the one genuine bloat source in the gate4 output.
# 60 files that pack to 36.9 MB: 58% of the entire tree-artifact footprint, more
# than everything else under candidate_phylogenetics/ combined. They are already
# gzipped so they do not compress further, and they are pure solver scratch --
# IQ-TREE writes tree.ckp.gz only so an interrupted search can resume. Nothing
# scientific is lost: the tree (tree.treefile, tree.contree), branch support
# (tree.splits.nex), model selection and fit (tree.iqtree, tree.model.gz), the
# ML distances (tree.mldist), the input alignment (aligned.fasta) and the exact
# IQ-TREE invocation including -B 1000 and --seed (tree.log) are all tracked.
*.ckp.gz

# The two top-level pipeline logs. Unlike every other artifact here they are
# rewritten wholesale on every run, so tracking them makes each rerun a large
# diff against the previous machine's timings rather than a result change.
# Nothing in them is secret -- the paths they embed are the project directory,
# with no username or home path -- and every figure that matters from them
# (record counts, isolate and triplet totals, pool sizes, per-phylogroup
# runtimes) is reproduced in README.md. Drop these two lines if you want them.
# Note this pattern is depth-1 only: the 60 per-candidate IQ-TREE tree.log files
# under output/ga_search/.../ are deliberately NOT matched and ARE tracked.
output/ortho_pipeline.log
output/ortho_phylogeny.log

# run_main.sh archives output/ to a sibling directory outside the repo.
# Adding the pattern here covers the case where someone runs it from inside the repo.
_pipeline_archive/
